na_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/ndruid/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 25, "playtime_forever": 46954, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 10771, "last_played": 1780255024, "avatar": "e9b21ad3e35c375be0b7837a6a998143b83fbe38"}, "language": "english", "review": "Great successor in the ARMA franchise. Especially the modding community carries the success of this game.\nWhile this is game is bug-hell come true, it is engaging and fun. \n\nThe one thing standing far out and making the result an negative rating in sum is the DLC selling strategy. \n\nIntrusive in-game advertising alone would be inacceptable for many, if the DLC items would just be added to the game. One could just not use them. But since they substitute items it destroys the immersion and some gameplay elements entirely when e.g. all enemies carry DLC items, which you can use theoretically, but with an ad window popping up in the middle of combat killing you. Just ignoring the items is a hard option since one sometimes rely on re-arming, which is actually an important fun part of the game. It tries to bully you into buying several expensive and uninteresting DLCs breaking the game for those who don't.\n\nTo the 28€ base game, it tries to force you to spend 34€ additionally for two DLCs (Marksmen and Contact).", "timestamp_created": 1569161902, "timestamp_updated": 1569162081, "voted_up": false, "votes_up": 1, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": "0.482386767864227295", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1378969200", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "55232090", "author": {"steamid": "76561198060327911", "personaname": "Olive", "persona_status": "in-game", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561198060327911/", "num_games_owned": 250, "num_reviews": 1, "playtime_forever": 74, "p